jobs.description:
We’re looking for a reach truck operator who is skilled at driving this type of equipment for a dynamic organization in the Echt region. In this role, you’ll be responsible for handling incoming and outgoing goods using a reach truck. Does working in a clean, well-organized facility energize you? This permanent position offers you job security on the day shift!

Duties:

- Placing pallets of products on shelves using a single-deep or double-deep reach truck;
- Picking orders; 
- Assisting with loading containers; 
- Supporting all logistical tasks as they arise.

You’ll spend most of your time operating the reach truck, so it’s important that you have experience with this type of logistics vehicle. Do you see yourself in this role? Don’t hesitate—read on!

This is a day shift position from 6:00 AM to 3:00 PM, Monday through Friday. 

- Experience operating a reach truck and a certificate demonstrating that you possess the qualities of a good reach truck operator;
- You speak Dutch, English, or German.

This is what you will do

You will be working at a large company in Zoetermeer where different types of meat products are produced that the whole of the Netherlands eats on their sandwich every morning. You can think of grill sausage, minced meat, filet american and much more! This organization has been active in the food industry for years and is a regular supplier of various supermarket chains throughout the Netherlands such as Jumbo, Lidl and Plus.

Within this company there is no slaughtering! The slaughtered meat within the production area is only processed into a final product that ends up in the supermarkets. This means you will be working in an environment where hygiene (NVWA and BRC) is very important!

As a Production Employee you will work together with your colleagues to produce various meat products according to the planning. The following tasks belong to your function:

- Packaging of meat products;
- Keeping track of the production process and assisting where necessary;
- Reading production receipts and planning;
- Checking articles for correct labels and shelf life;
- Producing according to the planning;
- Supplying machines;

You will be working in a day shift from Monday to Friday. The working hours may vary due to the supermarket orders. In any case, you will start at 06:00 or 07:00 in the morning and end your day between 15:00 and 17:00. After this you can enjoy the weekend and you are free!

This is who you are

- Living in the area of Rotterdam, Den Haag, Zoetermeer, Leiden, Waddinxveen, Capelle aan den IJssel, Alphen aan den Rijn or Woerden;
- Willing to work in a multicultural team;
- Willing to work fulltime and work overtime when there are rush orders;
- You speak the English or Dutch language;
- Able to perform work at a fast pace;
- You can be present every morning at 06:00 or 07:00.

Are you looking for a stable full-time job in logistics where you can combine working with a reach truck with a variety of warehouse activities? Do you enjoy a hands-on role, work accurately, and feel comfortable in an international team? Then this Warehouse Operative position could be a great next step for you.

You will work in a modern distribution centre in Hazeldonk, where you will operate a reach truck but also be involved in picking, packing, loading, unloading, and other warehouse activities. You will work in both English and Dutch and have the opportunity to build a long-term career in logistics.

What are you going to do?
As a Warehouse Operative, you play an important role in the daily warehouse operation. You will use your reach truck certificate to safely move and store goods, but your work will involve much more than operating a reach truck. Together with your colleagues, you make sure incoming and outgoing goods are processed accurately and efficiently.

Key Responsibilities:

- Operating a reach truck to move, store, and retrieve goods safely;
- Picking, packing, and preparing customer orders for dispatch;
- Loading and unloading goods and checking incoming shipments;
- Performing quality checks and verifying product quantities and accuracy;
- Carrying out various physical warehouse activities, including lifting and moving packages of approximately 20–30 kg;
- Supporting colleagues with other logistics activities when needed.

Working Hours:

- Monday to Friday;
- Day shift;
- Full-time position of 40 hours per week.

What do we offer?
You will join a professional international logistics environment where you can use your reach truck experience while gaining experience across different warehouse activities. The company offers a stable working environment and opportunities to develop within logistics.

Besides this, you will receive:

- Gross hourly salary of €14.99;
- Full-time employment of 40 hours per week;
- Long-term employment opportunities;
